WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Before you touch a single tool, you need to understand what HVAC systems
actually do.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
This lesson covers every tool in your HVAC toolkit and how to use each one
correctly. The digital multimeter measures voltage, resistance, continuity, and
capacitance — you will use it on every single service call. The clamp-on ammeter

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Multimeter: Measures voltage (V), resistance (Ω), continuity, and capacitance
(µF). The most-used diagnostic tool in HVAC.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Manifold Gauge Set: Two pressure gauges (blue=low side, red=high side) with
valves and hoses for measuring system pressures and charging refrigerant.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Clamp Meter: Measures amperage by clamping around a wire without disconnecting
it. Used to check motor amp draw against nameplate ratings.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Here's why this matters on the job: A technician without proper tools cannot
diagnose anything. Employers expect you to own a basic toolkit. Many WIOA
programs cover tool costs — take advantage of this.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Watch out for these: Always zero your multimeter before measuring resistance.
And — Never connect the high-side gauge hose to the low-side port — check the
line sizes

00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

